 r"I am writing to apply for the Product Analyst -- AI Enablement position at CAF Bank (reference EO206). I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have turned operational problems into AI use cases with clear outcomes, defined how to measure whether they work, and kept safety and governance at the centre of the design.",

 r"What attracts me most to CAF Bank is that the work has a visible end point: AI that helps a bank for charities serve its customers better, introduced safely in a regulated setting. The posting describes translating pain points into scoped use cases, producing requirements, preparing governance packs and tracking measurable benefits, which is very close to the work I have most enjoyed so far. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I worked out the logic after a few examples and proposed an AI use case: an agent built with Claude Code, with a validation step to check its accuracy. My supervisor was sceptical at first, but I delivered it before the same-day deadline. It cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent, and taught me that an AI solution only creates value once people trust its controls.",

